theory AdaSpark_Parser
  imports "../../Isabelle_Lex-Yacc/LexYacc" "AdaSpark_Ast"
begin

section\<open>Lexer and Parser for AdaSpark\<close>

text\<open>
  This theory contains the lexer and the parser of AdaSpark, generated by
  \<open>ml_lex_yacc [state]\<close> (the re-entrant variant of the library: every parse has
  its own state object), and \<^verbatim>\<open>AdaSpark_Parse\<close>, the parse driver. What is
  AdaSpark, and where does its grammar come from?

  \<^bold>\<open>SPARK 2014 is a subset of Ada 2012\<close>, and Ada 2012 has an official syntax:
  Annex P of the Ada Reference Manual, an EBNF grammar of the language.
  AdaSpark follows that syntax summary for the subset that SPARK uses, and
  leaves out the rest: generics, tasking and protected objects, \<open>goto\<close>
  and labels, interfaces, renamings, representation clauses other than
  attribute definitions, child unit subtleties, \<open>separate\<close> units. What the
  grammar covers:

  \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>compilation units\<close>: context clauses (\<open>with\<close>, \<open>limited with\<close>, \<open>private with\<close>,
    \<open>use\<close>, \<open>use type\<close>), package specifications (with a private part) and
    bodies, subprogram declarations and bodies, pragmas;
  \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>declarations\<close>: objects and constants, number declarations, exceptions,
    types (enumerations, signed and modular integers, floating and fixed
    point types, constrained and unconstrained arrays, records with
    discriminants and variant parts, tagged and derived types, private and
    limited private types, access types, incomplete types), subtypes,
    subprograms (procedures, functions, expression functions, null
    procedures, \<open>overriding\<close>), \<open>use\<close> clauses, pragmas, attribute definition
    clauses;
  \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>statements\<close>: \<open>null\<close>, assignment, procedure call, \<open>if\<close>, \<open>case\<close>, loops
    (\<open>while\<close>, \<open>for\<close> over ranges and over containers, \<open>reverse\<close>, named loops),
    blocks, \<open>exit\<close>, \<open>return\<close>, \<open>raise\<close>, exception handlers, pragmas;
  \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>expressions\<close>: the full expression language of Ada 2012 with its six levels
    of operator precedence (logical, relational, adding, unary adding,
    multiplying, highest), short-circuit operators, membership tests,
    attributes (\<open>X'First\<close>, \<open>F'Result\<close>, \<open>X'Old\<close>), qualified expressions,
    aggregates (positional, named, with \<open>others\<close>, extension and delta
    aggregates), slices, allocators, conditional expressions (\<open>if\<close> and
    \<open>case\<close>) and quantified expressions (\<open>for all\<close>, \<open>for some\<close>);
  \<^item> \<^bold>\<open>SPARK contracts\<close>: the aspect specifications \<open>with Pre => \<dots>, Post => \<dots>,
    Global => \<dots>, Depends => \<dots>, Contract_Cases => \<dots>, SPARK_Mode, Ghost\<close>,
    \<open>Type_Invariant\<close>, \<open>Default_Initial_Condition\<close>, \<open>Refined_State\<close>, \<open>\<dots>\<close>, on
    packages, subprograms, objects and types, and the SPARK pragmas
    (\<open>Assert\<close>, \<open>Loop_Invariant\<close>, \<open>Loop_Variant\<close>, \<open>Assume\<close>, \<open>Annotate\<close>). They
    are read as what they syntactically are in Ada 2012 - a name with an
    optional expression - so the grammar needs no knowledge of the contract
    language; its expressions are ordinary Ada expressions.

  \<^bold>\<open>Case.\<close> Ada is case insensitive. The lexer recognises the reserved words in
  any case, identifiers are kept as written, and the environment compares them
  in lower case.

  \<^bold>\<open>Comments\<close> start with \<open>--\<close> and run to the end of the line; they may contain
  antiquotations \<open>--@ tag[navi](level) \<open>body\<close>\<close>, attached to the node of the
  next real token, as in the other front-ends. The annotations of the older
  SPARK language (\<open>--# pre \<dots>\<close>) are plain comments.

  \<^bold>\<open>A deliberate limitation of the lexer.\<close> The apostrophe is both the attribute
  tick and the delimiter of a character literal. The lexer reads \<open>'x'\<close> as a
  character literal whenever three characters make one; a qualified expression
  whose operand is a parenthesised character literal, \<open>T'('a')\<close>, is therefore
  not read.

  \<^bold>\<open>No stream between lexer and parser.\<close> Ada needs none: there is no layout, the
  grammar is ordinary LALR(1) over the lexer's tokens. A conditional expression
  has no separate bracket of its own; it is an association inside the
  parentheses of its context, as in the Reference Manual.

  \<^bold>\<open>Conflicts and what is not read.\<close> The grammar has 11 shift/reduce conflicts
  and no reduce/reduce conflict; each is resolved by shifting, the reading the
  language intends. They come from six places: the keyword \<open>null\<close> (a null
  statement or the literal, and the \<open>not null\<close> of a subtype indication), the
  bar that extends the choices of a membership test, the range \<open>L .. H\<close> as an
  association against a choice, the commas that separate the alternatives of a
  \<open>case\<close> expression against those of an enclosing association list, \<open>not\<close>
  after a parameter's mode, and \<open>with\<close> after a derived type (a record
  extension, not an aspect list). A consequence is that \<open>X : not null T\<close> (a
  null-excluding object) and a derived type directly followed by aspects are
  not read. The logical operators \<open>and\<close>, \<open>or\<close> and \<open>xor\<close> share one precedence
  level and associate to the left, so \<open>A and B or C\<close>, which Ada forbids without
  parentheses, is accepted; \<open>**\<close> is non-associative, as in Ada, and
  \<open>2 ** 3 ** 4\<close> is rejected.
\<close>
ML\<open>
(* Everything the lexer and the grammar actions need to remember during one
   parse lives in one state object, created per parse ("init") and handed to
   the lexer (ML-Lex %arg) and the parser (ML-Yacc %arg) by "ml_lex_yacc
   [state]" - nothing is shared between parses.
     base        - the library's own part: source, context, position table
     pending     - comments lexed since the previous real token
     attached    - the comments that have been attached to a token position
     antiq_*     - the antiquotation scanner (see the lexer): nesting depth of
                   the cartouche being skipped, which comment state to return
                   to, the most recent tag, the body text so far and its start
                   position
     comment_depth, bodyless_ok
                 - block comments nest; whether a bodyless antiquotation tag
                   is allowed in the current comment
     lex_error   - the first lexical error (unterminated comment, string,
                   escape): the lexer cannot raise it itself, as the parse's
                   error callback decides how an error is reported (loudly, or
                   silently for the "_reject" commands), so it is recorded here
                   and reported by "AdaSpark_Parse.parse" when the parse is
                   over *)
structure AdaSpark_State = struct
  type comments = Position.T AdaSpark_Ast.comment list

  type T = {base : Lex_yacc_state.T,
            pending : comments Unsynchronized.ref,
            attached : (Position.T * comments) list Unsynchronized.ref,
            antiq_depth : int Unsynchronized.ref,
            antiq_from_block : bool Unsynchronized.ref,
            antiq_tag : (string * AdaSpark_Ast.navi list * int * Position.T)
              Unsynchronized.ref,
            antiq_buf : string list Unsynchronized.ref,
            antiq_start : Position.T Unsynchronized.ref,
            comment_depth : int Unsynchronized.ref,
            bodyless_ok : bool Unsynchronized.ref,
            comment_start : int Unsynchronized.ref,
            lex_error : (string * Position.T) option Unsynchronized.ref}

  fun init ctxt source : T =
    {base = Lex_yacc_state.init ctxt source,
     pending = Unsynchronized.ref [],
     attached = Unsynchronized.ref [],
     antiq_depth = Unsynchronized.ref 0,
     antiq_from_block = Unsynchronized.ref true,
     antiq_tag = Unsynchronized.ref ("", [], 0, Position.none),
     antiq_buf = Unsynchronized.ref [],
     antiq_start = Unsynchronized.ref Position.none,
     comment_depth = Unsynchronized.ref 0,
     bodyless_ok = Unsynchronized.ref false,
     comment_start = Unsynchronized.ref 0,
     lex_error = Unsynchronized.ref NONE}
end

(* The comments/antiquotations collected while lexing, attached to whichever
   real token follows (as in C11_Comments / Occam2_Comments / Scala3_Comments).
   *)
structure AdaSpark_Comments = struct
  fun push (st : AdaSpark_State.T) c = #pending st := !(#pending st) @ [c]

  fun push_raw st (text, pos) =
    if List.all Char.isSpace (String.explode text) then ()
    else push st (AdaSpark_Ast.Raw_txt [(text, pos)])

  fun push_antiquotation st tag navi level cartouche =
    push st (AdaSpark_Ast.Antiquotation (tag, navi, level, cartouche))

  fun attach_pending (st : AdaSpark_State.T) (p : Position.T) =
    (case !(#pending st) of
       [] => ()
     | cs => (#pending st := []; #attached st := (p, cs) :: !(#attached st)))

  (* Non-destructive on purpose, for the reason given at "C11_Comments.claim".
     *)
  fun claim (st : AdaSpark_State.T) (p : Position.T) : Position.T
    AdaSpark_Ast.comment list =
    (case AList.lookup (op =) (!(#attached st)) p of NONE => [] | SOME cs => cs)

  fun mk_nodeInfo st (claimed_at : Position.T)
    (report_pos : Position.T) : Position.T AdaSpark_Ast.nodeInfo =
    (case claim st claimed_at of
       [] => AdaSpark_Ast.OnlyPos report_pos
     | cs => AdaSpark_Ast.NodeInfo (cs, report_pos))
end

\<close>
SML_import \<open>structure AdaSpark_Ast = struct open AdaSpark_Ast end\<close>
SML_import \<open>structure AdaSpark_State = struct open AdaSpark_State end\<close>
SML_import \<open>structure AdaSpark_Comments = struct open AdaSpark_Comments end\<close>
ml_lex_yacc [verbose, state] "AdaSpark" where

lex_user_declarations\<open>
(* The lexer's and the parser's argument is the per-parse state of
   "AdaSpark_State" (the lexer rules and the grammar actions call it "st");
   "init" creates it, "base" is its part the library functions work on. *)
type arg = AdaSpark_State.T
fun init ctxt source : arg = AdaSpark_State.init ctxt source
fun base (st : arg) : Lex_yacc_state.T = #base st

fun gp (st : arg) yypos = Lex_yacc_state.get_pos (base st) yypos
fun report (st : arg) x = Lex_yacc_state.report_token (base st) x

fun antiq_depth (st : arg) = #antiq_depth st
fun antiq_from_block (st : arg) = #antiq_from_block st
fun antiq_tag (st : arg) = #antiq_tag st
fun antiq_buf (st : arg) = #antiq_buf st
fun antiq_start (st : arg) = #antiq_start st
fun comment_depth (st : arg) = #comment_depth st
fun bodyless_ok (st : arg) = #bodyless_ok st
fun comment_start (st : arg) = #comment_start st

(* Every real token goes through one of the constructors below, which, before
   reporting the token's markup, (1) let the comments gathered since the
   previous token attach themselves to this one, and (2) tell the layout
   recorder where this token starts and stops and what kind of token it is.
   Value-carrying tokens get their true start/end span as position. *)
fun stok st kind markup (yypos, yytext, cons) =
    (AdaSpark_Comments.attach_pending st (gp st yypos);
     tok (base st) (yypos, yytext, markup, kind, "", cons))

fun stok_val st kind markup (yypos, yytext, cons, value) =
    let
      val _ = AdaSpark_Comments.attach_pending st (gp st yypos)
      val p = gp st yypos
      val p' = gp st (yypos + String.size yytext)
      val _ = report st (yypos, String.size yytext, markup, kind, "")
    in cons (value, p, p') end


(* The reserved words of Ada 2012, in any case. The ones SPARK does not use
   (tasking, generics, "goto", ...) are lexed as RESERVED: the grammar has no
   rule for them, so they are syntax errors, but not lexical ones. *)
fun word_tok st (yypos, yytext) =
    let
      fun kw kind cons = stok st kind Markup.keyword1 (yypos, yytext, cons)
      fun rsv () = stok_val st "RESERVED" Markup.keyword1
                     (yypos, yytext, Tokens.RESERVED, yytext)
    in
      case String.map Char.toLower yytext of
        "abs" => kw "ABS" Tokens.ABS
      | "abstract" => kw "ABSTRACT" Tokens.ABSTRACT
      | "access" => kw "ACCESS" Tokens.ACCESS
      | "aliased" => kw "ALIASED" Tokens.ALIASED
      | "all" => kw "ALL" Tokens.ALL
      | "and" => kw "AND" Tokens.AND
      | "array" => kw "ARRAY" Tokens.ARRAY
      | "begin" => kw "BEGIN" Tokens.BEGIN
      | "body" => kw "BODY" Tokens.BODY
      | "case" => kw "CASE" Tokens.CASE
      | "constant" => kw "CONSTANT" Tokens.CONSTANT
      | "declare" => kw "DECLARE" Tokens.DECLARE
      | "delta" => kw "DELTA" Tokens.DELTA
      | "digits" => kw "DIGITS" Tokens.DIGITS
      | "else" => kw "ELSE" Tokens.ELSE
      | "elsif" => kw "ELSIF" Tokens.ELSIF
      | "end" => kw "END" Tokens.END
      | "exception" => kw "EXCEPTION" Tokens.EXCEPTION
      | "exit" => kw "EXIT" Tokens.EXIT
      | "for" => kw "FOR" Tokens.FOR
      | "function" => kw "FUNCTION" Tokens.FUNCTION
      | "if" => kw "IF" Tokens.IF
      | "in" => kw "IN" Tokens.IN
      | "is" => kw "IS" Tokens.IS
      | "limited" => kw "LIMITED" Tokens.LIMITED
      | "loop" => kw "LOOP" Tokens.LOOP
      | "mod" => kw "MOD" Tokens.MOD
      | "new" => kw "NEW" Tokens.NEW
      | "not" => kw "NOT" Tokens.NOT
      | "null" => kw "NULL" Tokens.NULL
      | "of" => kw "OF" Tokens.OF
      | "or" => kw "OR" Tokens.OR
      | "others" => kw "OTHERS" Tokens.OTHERS
      | "out" => kw "OUT" Tokens.OUT
      | "overriding" => kw "OVERRIDING" Tokens.OVERRIDING
      | "package" => kw "PACKAGE" Tokens.PACKAGE
      | "pragma" => kw "PRAGMA" Tokens.PRAGMA
      | "private" => kw "PRIVATE" Tokens.PRIVATE
      | "procedure" => kw "PROCEDURE" Tokens.PROCEDURE
      | "raise" => kw "RAISE" Tokens.RAISE
      | "range" => kw "RANGE" Tokens.RANGE
      | "record" => kw "RECORD" Tokens.RECORD
      | "rem" => kw "REM" Tokens.REM
      | "return" => kw "RETURN" Tokens.RETURN
      | "reverse" => kw "REVERSE" Tokens.REVERSE
      | "some" => kw "SOME" Tokens.SOME
      | "subtype" => kw "SUBTYPE" Tokens.SUBTYPE
      | "tagged" => kw "TAGGED" Tokens.TAGGED
      | "then" => kw "THEN" Tokens.THEN
      | "type" => kw "TYPE" Tokens.TYPE
      | "use" => kw "USE" Tokens.USE
      | "when" => kw "WHEN" Tokens.WHEN
      | "while" => kw "WHILE" Tokens.WHILE
      | "with" => kw "WITH" Tokens.WITH
      | "xor" => kw "XOR" Tokens.XOR
      | "abort" => rsv () | "accept" => rsv () | "at" => rsv ()
      | "delay" => rsv () | "do" => rsv () | "entry" => rsv ()
      | "generic" => rsv () | "goto" => rsv () | "interface" => rsv ()
      | "protected" => rsv () | "renames" => rsv () | "requeue" => rsv ()
      | "select" => rsv () | "separate" => rsv () | "synchronized" => rsv ()
      | "task" => rsv () | "terminate" => rsv () | "until" => rsv ()
      | _ => stok_val st "IDENT" Markup.free
          (yypos, yytext, Tokens.IDENT, yytext)
    end

(* Accumulate one fragment of raw comment text, tagged with its own span. *)
fun push_raw_fragment st (yypos, yytext) =
    AdaSpark_Comments.push_raw st
      (yytext, Position.range_position
       (gp st yypos, gp st (yypos + String.size yytext)))

fun char_to_navi #"u" = AdaSpark_Ast.up
  | char_to_navi #"U" = AdaSpark_Ast.Up
  | char_to_navi #"r" = AdaSpark_Ast.right
  | char_to_navi #"d" = AdaSpark_Ast.down
  | char_to_navi c = raise Fail ("invalid navigation character " ^ String.str c)

(* Splits the text matched after the leading "@" into the tag name, its optional
   bracketed navigation string, and its optional parenthesized level. *)
fun parse_tag_navi_level text =
    let
      val trim =
        Substring.string o Substring.dropr Char.isSpace o Substring.full
      val after_at =
        Substring.dropl (fn c => c = #"@" orelse Char.isSpace c)
          (Substring.full text)
      val (name_ss, rest1) =
        Substring.splitl (fn c => Char.isAlphaNum c orelse c = #"_") after_at
      val rest1' = Substring.dropl Char.isSpace rest1
      val (navi, rest2) =
        if Substring.size rest1' > 0 andalso Substring.sub (rest1', 0) =
          #"[" then
          let
            val (navi_ss, after) =
              Substring.splitl (fn c => c <> #"]") (Substring.triml 1 rest1')
          in (map char_to_navi (String.explode (Substring.string navi_ss)),
              Substring.triml 1 after) end
        else ([], rest1')
      val rest2' = Substring.dropl Char.isSpace rest2
      val level =
        if Substring.size rest2' > 0 andalso Substring.sub (rest2', 0) =
          #"(" then
          let val (lvl_ss, _) =
            Substring.splitl (fn c => c <> #")") (Substring.triml 1 rest2')
          in valOf (Int.fromString (Substring.string lvl_ss)) end
        else 0
    in (trim (Substring.string name_ss), navi, level) end

(* A bodyless tag is a complete antiquotation with the empty body - but only
   where the comment opener allowed it ("//@", "/*@"): elsewhere it is plain
   comment text and is dropped here. *)
fun antiq_flush_pending_tag st =
    let val (name, navi, level, pos) = !(antiq_tag st) in
      if name = "" then ()
      else
        (antiq_tag st := ("", [], 0, Position.none);
         if !(bodyless_ok st)
         then AdaSpark_Comments.push_antiquotation
           st {tag = (name, pos)} navi {level = level} {cartouche = ("", pos)}
         else ())
    end

fun antiq_tag_seen st (yypos, yytext) =
    let
      val (name, navi, level) = parse_tag_navi_level yytext
      val _ = if yypos = !(comment_start st) then bodyless_ok st := true else ()
    in antiq_flush_pending_tag st; antiq_tag
      st := (name, navi, level, gp st yypos) end

fun antiq_body_start st yypos = antiq_start st := gp st yypos

fun antiq_body_push st text = antiq_buf st := text :: !(antiq_buf st)

fun antiq_body_finish st yypos =
    let
      val body_text = String.concat (rev (!(antiq_buf st)))
      val body_pos = Position.range_position (!(antiq_start st), gp st yypos)
      val (tag_text, navi, level, tag_pos) = !(antiq_tag st)
    in
      antiq_buf st := [];
      antiq_tag st := ("", [], 0, Position.none);
      AdaSpark_Comments.push_antiquotation
        st {tag = (tag_text, tag_pos)} navi {level = level} {cartouche =
            (body_text, body_pos)}
    end

(* The quoted-string alternative to a cartouche body: tag, level and body in one
   rule. *)
fun antiq_tag_and_string_seen st (yypos, yytext) =
    let
      fun find_quote i = if String.sub (yytext, i) =
        #"\"" then i else find_quote (i + 1)
      val qpos = find_quote 0
      val (name, navi, level) =
        parse_tag_navi_level (String.substring (yytext, 0, qpos))
      val body_len = String.size yytext - qpos - 2
      val body_text = String.substring (yytext, qpos + 1, body_len)
      val body_start = yypos + qpos + 1
      val body_pos =
        Position.range_position
          (gp st body_start, gp st (body_start + body_len))
    in
      AdaSpark_Comments.push_antiquotation
        st {tag = (name, gp st yypos)} navi {level = level} {cartouche =
            (body_text, body_pos)}
    end

fun tag_with_body st (yypos, yytext) =
    (report st (yypos, String.size yytext, Markup.antiquote,
                "AdaSpark antiquotation tag+body", "");
     antiq_tag_and_string_seen st (yypos, yytext))

fun tag_only st (yypos, yytext) =
    (antiq_tag_seen st (yypos, yytext);
     if !(bodyless_ok st)
     then report st (yypos, String.size yytext, Markup.antiquote,
                     "AdaSpark antiquotation tag", "")
     else ())

fun cartouche_open st (yypos, yytext) block =
    (report st (yypos, String.size yytext, Markup.cartouche,
                "AdaSpark antiquotation body", "");
     antiq_depth st := 1; antiq_from_block st := block;
     antiq_body_start st (yypos + String.size yytext))


(* Comments run to the end of the line. *)
fun comment_open st yypos =
    (bodyless_ok st := false; comment_start st := yypos + 2;
     antiq_from_block st := false)

(* The first lexical error is recorded (see "AdaSpark_State"); the lexer
   carries on, and "AdaSpark_Parse.parse" reports it when the parse is over. *)
fun lex_fail (st : arg) (msg, pos) =
    (case !(#lex_error st) of NONE =>
     #lex_error st := SOME (msg, pos) | SOME _ => ())

(* Shadows the default "eof" of the "[state]" header: an unterminated
   antiquotation is a genuine error, reported at its own start. *)
fun eof (st : arg) =
    let
      val _ =
        if !(antiq_depth st) > 0
        then (antiq_depth st := 0;
              lex_fail st ("Unterminated antiquotation body: no matching " ^
                           "closing cartouche before the end of input",
                           !(antiq_start st)))
        else antiq_flush_pending_tag st
    in Tokens.EOF (Position.none, Position.none) end
\<close>
lex_definitions\<open>
D=[0-9];
N=[0-9][0-9_]*;
H=[0-9A-Fa-f];
HN=[0-9A-Fa-f][0-9A-Fa-f_]*;
LET=[A-Za-z];
LD=[A-Za-z0-9_];
TL=[A-Za-z_];
TA=[A-Za-z_0-9];
EXP=[eE][+\-]?{N};
HWS=[\ \t];
WS=[\ \t\r\n];
NAVI=[uUrd];
ATAG={HWS}*{TL}{TA}*({HWS}*"["{NAVI}*"]")?({HWS}*"("{D}+")")?;
ATAG={ATAG};
ES=(\\(["\\abfnrtv]|x{H}{H}));
OPENCART=\\\<open>;
CLOSECART=\\\<close>;
%s LCOMMENT ANTIQ;
\<close>
lex_rules\<open>
<INITIAL>"--"
        => (comment_open st yypos;
            YYBEGIN LCOMMENT;
            continue ());
<INITIAL>{WS}+                      => (continue ());

<INITIAL>"("
        => (stok st "LPAREN" Markup.delimiter (yypos, yytext, Tokens.LPAREN));
<INITIAL>")"
        => (stok st "RPAREN" Markup.delimiter (yypos, yytext, Tokens.RPAREN));
<INITIAL>","
        => (stok st "COMMA" Markup.delimiter (yypos, yytext, Tokens.COMMA));
<INITIAL>";"
        => (stok st "SEMI" Markup.delimiter (yypos, yytext, Tokens.SEMI));
<INITIAL>":"
        => (stok st "COLON" Markup.delimiter (yypos, yytext, Tokens.COLON));
<INITIAL>"."
        => (stok st "DOT" Markup.delimiter (yypos, yytext, Tokens.DOT));
<INITIAL>".."
        => (stok st "DOTDOT" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.DOTDOT));
<INITIAL>"=>"
        => (stok st "ARROW" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.ARROW));
<INITIAL>":="
        => (stok st "ASSIGN" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.ASSIGN));
<INITIAL>"'"
        => (stok st "TICK" Markup.delimiter (yypos, yytext, Tokens.TICK));
<INITIAL>"|"
        => (stok st "BAR" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.BAR));
<INITIAL>"!"
        => (stok st "BAR" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.BAR));
<INITIAL>"+"
        => (stok st "PLUS" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.PLUS));
<INITIAL>"-"
        => (stok st "MINUS" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.MINUS));
<INITIAL>"*"
        => (stok st "STAR" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.STAR));
<INITIAL>"/"
        => (stok st "SLASH" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.SLASH));
<INITIAL>"&"
        => (stok st "AMP" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.AMP));
<INITIAL>"**"
        => (stok st "EXP" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.EXP));
<INITIAL>"="
        => (stok st "EQ" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.EQ));
<INITIAL>"/="
        => (stok st "NE" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.NE));
<INITIAL>"<"
        => (stok st "LT" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.LT));
<INITIAL>"<="
        => (stok st "LE" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.LE));
<INITIAL>">"
        => (stok st "GT" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.GT));
<INITIAL>">="
        => (stok st "GE" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.GE));
<INITIAL>"<>"
        => (stok st "BOX" Markup.operator (yypos, yytext, Tokens.BOX));

<INITIAL>{LET}{LD}*                 => (word_tok st (yypos, yytext));

<INITIAL>{N}"#"{HN}"#"{EXP}?
        => (stok_val st "INT_LIT" Markup.numeral
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.INT_LIT, yytext));
<INITIAL>{N}"#"{HN}"."{HN}"#"{EXP}?
        => (stok_val st "REAL_LIT" Markup.numeral
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.REAL_LIT, yytext));
<INITIAL>{N}{EXP}?
        => (stok_val st "INT_LIT" Markup.numeral
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.INT_LIT, yytext));
<INITIAL>{N}"."{N}{EXP}?
        => (stok_val st "REAL_LIT" Markup.numeral
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.REAL_LIT, yytext));

<INITIAL>"'"[^\n']"'"
        => (stok_val st "CHAR_LIT" Markup.string
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.CHAR_LIT, yytext));
<INITIAL>"'''"
        => (stok_val st "CHAR_LIT" Markup.string
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.CHAR_LIT, yytext));
<INITIAL>["]([^"\n]|["]["])*["]
        => (stok_val st "STR_LIT" Markup.string
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.STR_LIT, yytext));
<INITIAL>.
        => (stok_val st "ILLEGAL" (Markup.bad ())
            (yypos, yytext, Tokens.ILLEGAL, yytext));

<LCOMMENT>[^@\\\n]+
        => (push_raw_fragment st (yypos, yytext);
            continue ());
<LCOMMENT>"@"{ATAG}{HWS}*["]([^"\\\n]|{ES})*["]
        => (tag_with_body st (yypos, yytext);
            continue ());
<LCOMMENT>"@"{ATAG}
        => (tag_only st (yypos, yytext);
            continue ());
<LCOMMENT>"@"
        => (push_raw_fragment st (yypos, yytext);
            continue ());
<LCOMMENT>"\\"
        => (push_raw_fragment st (yypos, yytext);
            continue ());
<LCOMMENT>{OPENCART}
        => (cartouche_open st (yypos, yytext) false;
            YYBEGIN ANTIQ;
            continue ());
<LCOMMENT>\n
        => (antiq_flush_pending_tag st;
            YYBEGIN INITIAL;
            continue ());

<ANTIQ>[^\\]+                       => (antiq_body_push st yytext; continue ());
<ANTIQ>"\\"                         => (antiq_body_push st yytext; continue ());
<ANTIQ>{OPENCART}
        => (antiq_depth st := !(antiq_depth st) + 1;
            antiq_body_push st yytext;
            continue ());
<ANTIQ>{CLOSECART}
        => (antiq_depth st := !(antiq_depth st) - 1;
            if !(antiq_depth st) = 0
              then (antiq_body_finish st yypos; YYBEGIN LCOMMENT; continue ())
                else (antiq_body_push st yytext; continue ()));
\<close>
and yacc_user_declarations\<open>
open AdaSpark_Ast

fun ndi st p = AdaSpark_Comments.mk_nodeInfo st p p
fun ndi2 st (p1, p2) =
  AdaSpark_Comments.mk_nodeInfo st p1 (Position.range_position (p1, p2))

(* A name token carries its true source span as its position, so the node's
   own range is exactly the name. *)
fun mkid st (s, l, r) = Ident (s, 0, ndi2 st (l, r))

(* "(e)" is a parenthesised expression, anything else in parentheses an
   aggregate. *)
fun paren_or_agg st (assocs, l, r) =
  (case assocs of
     [APos e] => EParen (e, ndi2 st (l, r))
   | _ => EAgg (assocs, ndi2 st (l, r)))

(* The statement forms that follow a name: used by the labelled loop and
   block rules. *)
fun label_loop st (lbl, scheme, body, l, r) =
  SLoop (SOME lbl, scheme, body, ndi2 st (l, r))
\<close>
yacc_definitions\<open>
%eop EOF
%arg (st) : AdaSpark_State.T
%noshift EOF

%left AND OR XOR
%nonassoc EQ NE LT LE GT GE IN NOT
%left PLUS MINUS AMP
%left UNARYADD
%left STAR SLASH MOD REM
%nonassoc EXP
%left HIGH
%left DOT TICK LPAREN

%term
        IDENT of string | INT_LIT of string | REAL_LIT of string
      | CHAR_LIT of string | STR_LIT of string | RESERVED of string
      | ILLEGAL of string
      | ABS | ABSTRACT | ACCESS | ALIASED | ALL | AND | ARRAY | BEGIN | BODY
          | CASE
      | CONSTANT | DECLARE | DELTA | DIGITS | ELSE | ELSIF | END | EXCEPTION
      | EXIT | FOR | FUNCTION | IF | IN | IS | LIMITED | LOOP | MOD | NEW | NOT
      | NULL | OF | OR | OTHERS | OUT | OVERRIDING | PACKAGE | PRAGMA | PRIVATE
      | PROCEDURE | RAISE | RANGE | RECORD | REM | RETURN | REVERSE | SOME
      | SUBTYPE | TAGGED | THEN | TYPE | USE | WHEN | WHILE | WITH | XOR
      | LPAREN | RPAREN | COMMA | SEMI | COLON | DOT | DOTDOT | ARROW | ASSIGN
      | TICK | BAR | PLUS | MINUS | STAR | SLASH | AMP | EXP | EQ | NE | LT
      | LE | GT | GE | BOX
      | UNARYADD | HIGH
      | ENTRY_CRATE | ENTRY_EXPR | ENTRY_TYPE | ENTRY_ID | ENTRY_BODY | EOF

%nonterm
        start_rule of Position.T root option
      |        name of Position.T ident
      |        attr_id of Position.T ident
      |        elit of Position.T ident
      |        desig of Position.T ident
      |        exprs of Position.T aExpr list
      |        pragma_args of Position.T aAssoc list
      |        ident_list of Position.T ident list
      |        elit_list of Position.T ident list
      |        expr of Position.T aExpr
      |        assoc of Position.T aAssoc
      |        assocs of Position.T aAssoc list
      |        choice of Position.T aChoice
      |        choices of Position.T aChoice list
      |        elsifs of (Position.T aExpr * Position.T aExpr) list
      |        opt_else of Position.T aExpr option
      |        case_alt of Position.T aChoice list * Position.T aExpr
      |        case_alts of (Position.T aChoice list * Position.T aExpr) list
      |        sub_ind of Position.T aSub
      |        drange of Position.T aDiscRange
      |        iter of Position.T aIter
      |        aspect of Position.T aAspect
      |        aspects of Position.T aAspect list
      |        opt_aspects of Position.T aAspect list
      |        idx of Position.T aIdx
      |        idxs of Position.T aIdx list
      |        component of Position.T aComponent
      |        components of Position.T aComponent list
      |        recdef of Position.T aRecDef
      |        variant_part of Position.T aVariantPart option
      |        variant_alts
          of (Position.T aChoice list * Position.T aRecDef) list
      |        typeprefix of bool * bool * bool
      |        typedef of Position.T aTypeDef
      |        param of Position.T aParam
      |        params of Position.T aParam list
      |        opt_discs of Position.T aParam list
      |        mode of mode
      |        opt_default of Position.T aExpr option
      |        spec of Position.T aSpec
      |        subp of Position.T aDecl
      |        subp_rest of Position.T aSpec -> Position.T aAspect list
          -> Position.T -> Position.T aDecl
      |        obj_decl of Position.T aDecl
      |        obj_tail of Position.T ident list -> Position.T
          -> Position.T aDecl
      |        obj_def_init of bool * bool -> Position.T ident list
          -> Position.T -> Position.T aDecl
      |        obj_def of Position.T aObjDef
      |        opt_assign of Position.T aExpr option
      |        decl of Position.T aDecl
      |        decls of Position.T aDecl list
      |        pkg of Position.T aDecl
      |        opt_private of Position.T aDecl list
      |        opt_init
          of (Position.T aStmt list * Position.T aHandler list) option
      |        opt_end_name of unit
      |        stmt of Position.T aStmt
      |        stmts of Position.T aStmt list
      |        elsif_stmts of (Position.T aExpr * Position.T aStmt list) list
      |        opt_else_stmts of Position.T aStmt list option
      |        alt of Position.T aChoice list * Position.T aStmt list
      |        alts of (Position.T aChoice list * Position.T aStmt list) list
      |        scheme of Position.T option * Position.T aScheme
      |        handler of Position.T aHandler
      |        handlers of Position.T aHandler list
      |        opt_handlers of Position.T aHandler list
      |        opt_label of Position.T ident option
      |        clause of Position.T aClause
      |        clauses of Position.T aClause list
      |        unit of Position.T aUnit
      |        crate of Position.T aUnit list
      |        lib_item of Position.T aDecl
\<close>
yacc_rules\<open>
start_rule:
        ENTRY_CRATE crate
        (SOME (Crate crate))
|       ENTRY_EXPR expr
        (SOME (Expr expr))
|       ENTRY_TYPE sub_ind
        (SOME (Type sub_ind))
|       ENTRY_ID name
        (SOME (Id name))
|       ENTRY_BODY stmts
        (SOME (Body stmts))
name:
        IDENT
        (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright))
desig:
        IDENT
        (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright))
|       STR_LIT
        (mkid st (STR_LIT, STR_LITleft, STR_LITright))
attr_id:
        IDENT
        (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright))
|       RANGE
        (mkid st ("Range", RANGEleft, RANGEright))
|       ACCESS
        (mkid st ("Access", ACCESSleft, ACCESSright))
|       DIGITS
        (mkid st ("Digits", DIGITSleft, DIGITSright))
|       DELTA
        (mkid st ("Delta", DELTAleft, DELTAright))
|       MOD
        (mkid st ("Mod", MODleft, MODright))
elit:
        IDENT
        (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright))
|       CHAR_LIT
        (mkid st (CHAR_LIT, CHAR_LITleft, CHAR_LITright))
ident_list:
        name
        ([name])
|       ident_list COMMA name
        (ident_list @ [name])
elit_list:
        elit
        ([elit])
|       elit_list COMMA elit
        (elit_list @ [elit])
exprs:
        expr
        ([expr])
|       exprs COMMA expr
        (exprs @ [expr])
choice:
        expr %prec IN
        (ChExpr expr)
|       expr DOTDOT expr %prec IN
        (ChRange (expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       OTHERS
        (ChOthers (ndi2 st (OTHERSleft, OTHERSright)))
choices:
        choice
        ([choice])
|       choices BAR choice
        (choices @ [choice])
assoc:
        expr
        (APos expr)
|       expr DOTDOT expr
        (ARange (expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       choices ARROW expr
        (ANamed (choices, expr, ndi2 st (choicesleft, exprright)))
|       IF expr THEN expr elsifs opt_else
        (APos (EIf ((expr1, expr2) :: elsifs, opt_else,
                    ndi2 st (IFleft, expr2right))))
|       CASE expr IS case_alts
        (APos (ECase (expr, case_alts, ndi2 st (CASEleft, case_altsright))))
|       FOR ALL IDENT IN drange ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (true, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterIn (false, drange), expr,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, exprright))))
|       FOR SOME IDENT IN drange ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (false, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterIn (false, drange), expr,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, exprright))))
|       FOR ALL IDENT IN REVERSE drange ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (true, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterIn (true, drange), expr,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, exprright))))
|       FOR SOME IDENT IN REVERSE drange ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (false, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterIn (true, drange), expr,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, exprright))))
|       FOR ALL IDENT OF REVERSE expr ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (true, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterOf (true, expr1), expr2,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, expr2right))))
|       FOR SOME IDENT OF REVERSE expr ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (false, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterOf (true, expr1), expr2,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, expr2right))))
|       FOR ALL IDENT OF expr ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (true, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterOf (false, expr1), expr2,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, expr2right))))
|       FOR SOME IDENT OF expr ARROW expr
        (APos (EQuant (false, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                       IterOf (false, expr1), expr2,
                       ndi2 st (FORleft, expr2right))))
assocs:
        assoc
        ([assoc])
|       assocs COMMA assoc
        (assocs @ [assoc])
elsifs:
        
        ([])
|       elsifs ELSIF expr THEN expr
        (elsifs @ [(expr1, expr2)])
opt_else:
        
        (NONE)
|       ELSE expr
        (SOME expr)
case_alt:
        WHEN choices ARROW expr
        ((choices, expr))
case_alts:
        case_alt
        ([case_alt])
|       case_alts COMMA case_alt
        (case_alts @ [case_alt])
expr:
        IDENT
        (EId (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright)))
|       INT_LIT
        (EInt (INT_LIT, ndi2 st (INT_LITleft, INT_LITright)))
|       REAL_LIT
        (EReal (REAL_LIT, ndi2 st (REAL_LITleft, REAL_LITright)))
|       CHAR_LIT
        (EChar (CHAR_LIT, ndi2 st (CHAR_LITleft, CHAR_LITright)))
|       STR_LIT
        (EStr (STR_LIT, ndi2 st (STR_LITleft, STR_LITright)))
|       NULL
        (ENull (ndi2 st (NULLleft, NULLright)))
|       expr DOT IDENT %prec DOT
        (ESel (expr, mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
               ndi2 st (exprleft, IDENTright)))
|       expr DOT ALL %prec DOT
        (EDeref (expr, ndi2 st (exprleft, ALLright)))
|       expr LPAREN assocs RPAREN
        (EApply (expr, assocs, ndi2 st (exprleft, RPARENright)))
|       expr TICK attr_id
        (EAttr (expr, attr_id, ndi2 st (exprleft, attr_idright)))
|       expr TICK LPAREN assocs RPAREN
        (EQual (expr, assocs, ndi2 st (exprleft, RPARENright)))
|       LPAREN assocs RPAREN
        (paren_or_agg st (assocs, LPARENleft, RPARENright))
|       LPAREN expr WITH assocs RPAREN
        (EExtAgg (expr, assocs, ndi2 st (LPARENleft, RPARENright)))
|       LPAREN expr WITH DELTA assocs RPAREN
        (EDeltaAgg (expr, assocs, ndi2 st (LPARENleft, RPARENright)))
|       NEW expr %prec HIGH
        (ENew (expr, ndi2 st (NEWleft, exprright)))
|       NOT expr %prec HIGH
        (EUn (Not, expr, ndi2 st (NOTleft, exprright)))
|       ABS expr %prec HIGH
        (EUn (Abs, expr, ndi2 st (ABSleft, exprright)))
|       MINUS expr %prec UNARYADD
        (EUn (UMinus, expr, ndi2 st (MINUSleft, exprright)))
|       PLUS expr %prec UNARYADD
        (EUn (UPlus, expr, ndi2 st (PLUSleft, exprright)))
|       expr PLUS expr
        (EBin (Plus, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr MINUS expr
        (EBin (Minus, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr AMP expr
        (EBin (Concat, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr STAR expr
        (EBin (Mul, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr SLASH expr
        (EBin (Div, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr MOD expr
        (EBin (Mod, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr REM expr
        (EBin (Rem, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr EXP expr
        (EBin (Exp, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr EQ expr
        (EBin (Eq, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr NE expr
        (EBin (Ne, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr LT expr
        (EBin (Lt, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr LE expr
        (EBin (Le, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr GT expr
        (EBin (Gt, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr GE expr
        (EBin (Ge, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr AND expr
        (EBin (And, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr OR expr
        (EBin (Or, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr XOR expr
        (EBin (Xor, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr AND THEN expr %prec AND
        (EBin (AndThen, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr OR ELSE expr %prec OR
        (EBin (OrElse, expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr IN choices
        (EIn (false, expr, choices, ndi2 st (exprleft, choicesright)))
|       expr NOT IN choices %prec IN
        (EIn (true, expr, choices, ndi2 st (exprleft, choicesright)))
sub_ind:
        expr
        (Sub (false, expr, NONE, nodeInfo_of_expr expr))
|       expr RANGE expr DOTDOT expr
        (Sub (false, expr1, SOME (expr2, expr3),
              ndi2 st (expr1left, expr3right)))
|       NOT NULL expr
        (Sub (true, expr, NONE, ndi2 st (NOTleft, exprright)))
drange:
        expr DOTDOT expr
        (DRRange (expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       sub_ind
        (DRSub sub_ind)
aspect:
        IDENT
        (Aspect (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright), NONE, NONE,
                 ndi2 st (IDENTleft, IDENTright)))
|       IDENT ARROW expr
        (Aspect (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright), NONE, SOME expr,
                 ndi2 st (IDENTleft, exprright)))
|       IDENT TICK IDENT ARROW expr
        (Aspect (mkid st (IDENT1, IDENT1left, IDENT1right),
                 SOME (mkid st (IDENT2, IDENT2left, IDENT2right)),
                 SOME expr, ndi2 st (IDENT1left, exprright)))
aspects:
        aspect
        ([aspect])
|       aspects COMMA aspect
        (aspects @ [aspect])
opt_aspects:
        
        ([])
|       WITH aspects
        (aspects)
idx:
        expr DOTDOT expr
        (IdxRange (expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, expr2right)))
|       expr
        (IdxSub expr)
|       expr RANGE BOX
        (IdxUnconstrained (expr, ndi2 st (exprleft, BOXright)))
idxs:
        idx
        ([idx])
|       idxs COMMA idx
        (idxs @ [idx])
opt_assign:
        
        (NONE)
|       ASSIGN expr
        (SOME expr)
component:
        ident_list COLON sub_ind opt_assign SEMI
        (Comp (ident_list, false, sub_ind, opt_assign,
               ndi2 st (ident_listleft, SEMIright)))
|       ident_list COLON ALIASED sub_ind opt_assign SEMI
        (Comp (ident_list, true, sub_ind, opt_assign,
               ndi2 st (ident_listleft, SEMIright)))
components:
        
        ([])
|       components component
        (components @ [component])
recdef:
        NULL SEMI
        (RecNull)
|       components variant_part
        (RecComps (components, variant_part))
variant_part:
        
        (NONE)
|       CASE name IS variant_alts END CASE SEMI
        (SOME (VariantPart (name, variant_alts, ndi2 st (CASEleft, SEMIright))))
variant_alts:
        WHEN choices ARROW recdef
        ([(choices, recdef)])
|       variant_alts WHEN choices ARROW recdef
        (variant_alts @ [(choices, recdef)])
typeprefix:
        
        ((false, false, false))
|       ABSTRACT
        ((true, false, false))
|       TAGGED
        ((false, true, false))
|       LIMITED
        ((false, false, true))
|       ABSTRACT TAGGED
        ((true, true, false))
|       ABSTRACT LIMITED
        ((true, false, true))
|       TAGGED LIMITED
        ((false, true, true))
|       ABSTRACT TAGGED LIMITED
        ((true, true, true))
typedef:
        LPAREN elit_list RPAREN
        (TEnum elit_list)
|       RANGE expr DOTDOT expr
        (TRange (expr1, expr2))
|       MOD expr
        (TMod expr)
|       DIGITS expr
        (TDigits (expr, NONE))
|       DIGITS expr RANGE expr DOTDOT expr
        (TDigits (expr1, SOME (expr2, expr3)))
|       DELTA expr
        (TDelta (expr, NONE))
|       DELTA expr RANGE expr DOTDOT expr
        (TDelta (expr1, SOME (expr2, expr3)))
|       ARRAY LPAREN idxs RPAREN OF sub_ind
        (TArray (idxs, false, sub_ind))
|       ARRAY LPAREN idxs RPAREN OF ALIASED sub_ind
        (TArray (idxs, true, sub_ind))
|       typeprefix RECORD recdef END RECORD
        (TRecord (#1 typeprefix, #2 typeprefix, #3 typeprefix, recdef))
|       typeprefix NULL RECORD
        (TRecord (#1 typeprefix, #2 typeprefix, #3 typeprefix, RecNull))
|       typeprefix NEW sub_ind
        (TDerived (#1 typeprefix, #3 typeprefix, sub_ind, ExtNone))
|       typeprefix NEW sub_ind WITH RECORD recdef END RECORD
        (TDerived (#1 typeprefix, #3 typeprefix, sub_ind, ExtRecord recdef))
|       typeprefix NEW sub_ind WITH NULL RECORD
        (TDerived (#1 typeprefix, #3 typeprefix, sub_ind, ExtRecord RecNull))
|       typeprefix NEW sub_ind WITH PRIVATE
        (TDerived (#1 typeprefix, #3 typeprefix, sub_ind, ExtPrivate))
|       typeprefix PRIVATE
        (TPrivate (#1 typeprefix, #2 typeprefix, #3 typeprefix))
|       ACCESS sub_ind
        (TAccess (false, AccPlain, sub_ind))
|       ACCESS ALL sub_ind
        (TAccess (false, AccAll, sub_ind))
|       ACCESS CONSTANT sub_ind
        (TAccess (false, AccConstant, sub_ind))
|       NOT NULL ACCESS sub_ind
        (TAccess (true, AccPlain, sub_ind))
|       NOT NULL ACCESS ALL sub_ind
        (TAccess (true, AccAll, sub_ind))
|       NOT NULL ACCESS CONSTANT sub_ind
        (TAccess (true, AccConstant, sub_ind))
mode:
        
        (MDefault)
|       IN
        (MIn)
|       OUT
        (MOut)
|       IN OUT
        (MInOut)
|       ACCESS
        (MAccess)
opt_default:
        
        (NONE)
|       ASSIGN expr
        (SOME expr)
param:
        ident_list COLON mode sub_ind opt_default
        (Param (ident_list, mode, sub_ind, opt_default,
                ndi2 st (ident_listleft, sub_indright)))
|       ident_list COLON NOT NULL ACCESS expr opt_default
        (Param (ident_list, MAccess,
                Sub (true, expr, NONE, nodeInfo_of_expr expr),
                opt_default, ndi2 st (ident_listleft, exprright)))
params:
        param
        ([param])
|       params SEMI param
        (params @ [param])
opt_discs:
        
        ([])
|       LPAREN params RPAREN
        (params)
spec:
        PROCEDURE name
        (Spec (false, false, name, [], NONE,
               ndi2 st (PROCEDUREleft, nameright)))
|       PROCEDURE name LPAREN params RPAREN
        (Spec (false, false, name, params, NONE,
               ndi2 st (PROCEDUREleft, RPARENright)))
|       FUNCTION desig RETURN sub_ind
        (Spec (false, true, desig, [], SOME sub_ind,
               ndi2 st (FUNCTIONleft, sub_indright)))
|       FUNCTION desig LPAREN params RPAREN RETURN sub_ind
        (Spec (false, true, desig, params, SOME sub_ind,
               ndi2 st (FUNCTIONleft, sub_indright)))
|       OVERRIDING PROCEDURE name
        (Spec (true, false, name, [], NONE,
               ndi2 st (OVERRIDINGleft, nameright)))
|       OVERRIDING PROCEDURE name LPAREN params RPAREN
        (Spec (true, false, name, params, NONE,
               ndi2 st (OVERRIDINGleft, RPARENright)))
|       OVERRIDING FUNCTION desig RETURN sub_ind
        (Spec (true, true, desig, [], SOME sub_ind,
               ndi2 st (OVERRIDINGleft, sub_indright)))
|       OVERRIDING FUNCTION desig LPAREN params RPAREN RETURN sub_ind
        (Spec (true, true, desig, params, SOME sub_ind,
               ndi2 st (OVERRIDINGleft, sub_indright)))
subp:
        spec opt_aspects subp_rest
        (subp_rest spec opt_aspects specleft)
subp_rest:
        SEMI
        (fn sp => fn asps => fn l =>
           DSpec (sp, false, asps, ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
|       IS NULL opt_aspects SEMI
        (fn sp => fn asps => fn l =>
           DNullProc (sp, asps @ opt_aspects, ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
|       IS ABSTRACT opt_aspects SEMI
        (fn sp => fn asps => fn l =>
           DSpec (sp, true, asps @ opt_aspects, ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
|       IS LPAREN assocs RPAREN opt_aspects SEMI
        (fn sp => fn asps => fn l =>
           DExprFun (sp,
                     (case assocs of
                        [APos e] => e
                      | _ => EAgg (assocs,
                                   ndi2 st (LPARENleft, RPARENright))),
                     asps @ opt_aspects, ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
|       IS decls BEGIN stmts opt_handlers END opt_end_name SEMI
        (fn sp => fn asps => fn l =>
           DBody (sp, asps, decls, stmts, opt_handlers,
                  ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
opt_end_name:
        
        (())
|       expr
        (())
obj_decl:
        ident_list COLON obj_tail
        (obj_tail ident_list ident_listleft)
obj_tail:
        ALIASED CONSTANT obj_def_init
        (fn ids => fn l => obj_def_init (true, true) ids l)
|       ALIASED obj_def_init
        (fn ids => fn l => obj_def_init (true, false) ids l)
|       CONSTANT ASSIGN expr SEMI
        (fn ids => fn l => DNumber (ids, expr, ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
|       CONSTANT obj_def_init
        (fn ids => fn l => obj_def_init (false, true) ids l)
|       obj_def_init
        (fn ids => fn l => obj_def_init (false, false) ids l)
|       EXCEPTION SEMI
        (fn ids => fn l => DException (ids, ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
obj_def_init:
        obj_def opt_assign opt_aspects SEMI
        (fn (al, cst) => fn ids => fn l =>
           DObject (ids, al, cst, obj_def, opt_assign, opt_aspects,
                    ndi2 st (l, SEMIright)))
obj_def:
        sub_ind
        (OSub sub_ind)
|       ARRAY LPAREN idxs RPAREN OF sub_ind
        (OArray (idxs, false, sub_ind))
|       ARRAY LPAREN idxs RPAREN OF ALIASED sub_ind
        (OArray (idxs, true, sub_ind))
pragma_args:
        
        ([])
|       LPAREN assocs RPAREN
        (assocs)
decl:
        obj_decl
        (obj_decl)
|       TYPE name opt_discs IS typedef opt_aspects SEMI
        (DType (name, opt_discs, typedef, opt_aspects,
                ndi2 st (TYPEleft, SEMIright)))
|       TYPE name SEMI
        (DIncomplete (name, ndi2 st (TYPEleft, SEMIright)))
|       SUBTYPE name IS sub_ind opt_aspects SEMI
        (DSubtype (name, sub_ind, opt_aspects,
                   ndi2 st (SUBTYPEleft, SEMIright)))
|       subp
        (subp)
|       pkg
        (pkg)
|       USE exprs SEMI
        (DUse (false, exprs, ndi2 st (USEleft, SEMIright)))
|       USE TYPE exprs SEMI
        (DUse (true, exprs, ndi2 st (USEleft, SEMIright)))
|       PRAGMA name pragma_args SEMI
        (DPragma (name, pragma_args, ndi2 st (PRAGMAleft, SEMIright)))
|       FOR expr USE expr SEMI
        (DAttrDef (expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (FORleft, SEMIright)))
decls:
        
        ([])
|       decls decl
        (decls @ [decl])
pkg:
        PACKAGE expr opt_aspects IS decls opt_private END opt_end_name SEMI
        (DPackage (expr, opt_aspects, decls, opt_private,
                   ndi2 st (PACKAGEleft, SEMIright)))
|       PACKAGE BODY expr opt_aspects IS decls opt_init END opt_end_name SEMI
        (DPackageBody (expr, opt_aspects, decls, opt_init,
                       ndi2 st (PACKAGEleft, SEMIright)))
opt_private:
        
        ([])
|       PRIVATE decls
        (decls)
opt_init:
        
        (NONE)
|       BEGIN stmts opt_handlers
        (SOME (stmts, opt_handlers))
opt_label:
        
        (NONE)
|       name
        (SOME name)
scheme:
        
        ((NONE, LoopPlain))
|       WHILE expr
        ((SOME WHILEleft, LoopWhile expr))
|       FOR IDENT IN drange
        ((SOME FORleft, LoopFor (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                                 IterIn (false, drange))))
|       FOR IDENT IN REVERSE drange
        ((SOME FORleft, LoopFor (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                                 IterIn (true, drange))))
|       FOR IDENT OF expr
        ((SOME FORleft, LoopFor (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                                 IterOf (false, expr))))
|       FOR IDENT OF REVERSE expr
        ((SOME FORleft, LoopFor (mkid st (IDENT, IDENTleft, IDENTright),
                                 IterOf (true, expr))))
elsif_stmts:
        
        ([])
|       elsif_stmts ELSIF expr THEN stmts
        (elsif_stmts @ [(expr, stmts)])
opt_else_stmts:
        
        (NONE)
|       ELSE stmts
        (SOME stmts)
alt:
        WHEN choices ARROW stmts
        ((choices, stmts))
alts:
        alt
        ([alt])
|       alts alt
        (alts @ [alt])
handler:
        WHEN choices ARROW stmts
        (Handler (choices, stmts, ndi2 st (WHENleft, stmtsright)))
handlers:
        handler
        ([handler])
|       handlers handler
        (handlers @ [handler])
opt_handlers:
        
        ([])
|       EXCEPTION handlers
        (handlers)
stmts:
        
        ([])
|       stmts stmt
        (stmts @ [stmt])
stmt:
        NULL SEMI
        (SNull (ndi2 st (NULLleft, SEMIright)))
|       expr ASSIGN expr SEMI
        (SAssign (expr1, expr2, ndi2 st (expr1left, SEMIright)))
|       expr SEMI
        (SCall (expr, ndi2 st (exprleft, SEMIright)))
|       IF expr THEN stmts elsif_stmts opt_else_stmts END IF SEMI
        (SIf ((expr, stmts) :: elsif_stmts, opt_else_stmts,
              ndi2 st (IFleft, SEMIright)))
|       CASE expr IS alts END CASE SEMI
        (SCase (expr, alts, ndi2 st (CASEleft, SEMIright)))
|       scheme LOOP stmts END LOOP opt_label SEMI
        (SLoop (NONE, #2 scheme, stmts,
               ndi2 st (case #1 scheme of SOME p => p | NONE => LOOP1left,
                        SEMIright)))
|       name COLON scheme LOOP stmts END LOOP opt_label SEMI
        (SLoop (SOME name, #2 scheme, stmts, ndi2 st (nameleft, SEMIright)))
|       DECLARE decls BEGIN stmts opt_handlers END opt_label SEMI
        (SBlock (NONE, decls, stmts, opt_handlers,
                 ndi2 st (DECLAREleft, SEMIright)))
|       BEGIN stmts opt_handlers END opt_label SEMI
        (SBlock (NONE, [], stmts, opt_handlers,
                 ndi2 st (BEGINleft, SEMIright)))
|       name COLON DECLARE decls BEGIN stmts opt_handlers END opt_label SEMI
        (SBlock (SOME name, decls, stmts, opt_handlers,
                 ndi2 st (nameleft, SEMIright)))
|       name COLON BEGIN stmts opt_handlers END opt_label SEMI
        (SBlock (SOME name, [], stmts, opt_handlers,
                 ndi2 st (nameleft, SEMIright)))
|       EXIT SEMI
        (SExit (NONE, NONE, ndi2 st (EXITleft, SEMIright)))
|       EXIT expr SEMI
        (SExit (SOME expr, NONE, ndi2 st (EXITleft, SEMIright)))
|       EXIT WHEN expr SEMI
        (SExit (NONE, SOME expr, ndi2 st (EXITleft, SEMIright)))
|       EXIT expr WHEN expr SEMI
        (SExit (SOME expr1, SOME expr2, ndi2 st (EXITleft, SEMIright)))
|       RETURN SEMI
        (SReturn (NONE, ndi2 st (RETURNleft, SEMIright)))
|       RETURN expr SEMI
        (SReturn (SOME expr, ndi2 st (RETURNleft, SEMIright)))
|       RAISE SEMI
        (SRaise (NONE, NONE, ndi2 st (RAISEleft, SEMIright)))
|       RAISE expr SEMI
        (SRaise (SOME expr, NONE, ndi2 st (RAISEleft, SEMIright)))
|       RAISE expr WITH expr SEMI
        (SRaise (SOME expr1, SOME expr2, ndi2 st (RAISEleft, SEMIright)))
|       PRAGMA name pragma_args SEMI
        (SPragma (name, pragma_args, ndi2 st (PRAGMAleft, SEMIright)))
clause:
        WITH exprs SEMI
        (CWith (false, false, exprs, ndi2 st (WITHleft, SEMIright)))
|       LIMITED WITH exprs SEMI
        (CWith (true, false, exprs, ndi2 st (LIMITEDleft, SEMIright)))
|       PRIVATE WITH exprs SEMI
        (CWith (false, true, exprs, ndi2 st (PRIVATEleft, SEMIright)))
|       USE exprs SEMI
        (CUse (false, exprs, ndi2 st (USEleft, SEMIright)))
|       USE TYPE exprs SEMI
        (CUse (true, exprs, ndi2 st (USEleft, SEMIright)))
clauses:
        
        ([])
|       clauses clause
        (clauses @ [clause])
lib_item:
        pkg
        (pkg)
|       subp
        (subp)
unit:
        clauses lib_item
        (Unit (clauses, lib_item,
               ndi2 st (case clauses of [] => lib_itemleft | _ => clausesleft,
                        lib_itemright)))
|       PRAGMA name pragma_args SEMI
        (Unit ([], DPragma (name, pragma_args,
                            ndi2 st (PRAGMAleft, SEMIright)),
               ndi2 st (PRAGMAleft, SEMIright)))
crate:
        
        ([])
|       crate unit
        (crate @ [unit])
\<close>

text\<open>
  \<^verbatim>\<open>AdaSpark_Parse\<close> runs the generated lexer/parser pair on a source, from one
  of five entry points (a source file, an expression, a subtype indication, a
  name, a sequence of statements: a synthetic first token selects the
  grammar's start). Every call creates its own \<^verbatim>\<open>AdaSpark_State\<close>, so calls are
  independent and may run concurrently. Unlike the Rust, Scala and occam
  front-ends there is no stream between lexer and parser that decides
  anything: the parser reads the lexer's tokens directly, after the entry
  token.
\<close>

ML\<open>
structure AdaSpark_Parse = struct

structure P = AdaSpark.AdaSparkParser
structure T = AdaSpark.AdaSparkLrVals.Tokens

datatype entry = Entry_Crate | Entry_Expr | Entry_Type | Entry_Id | Entry_Body

fun entry_token Entry_Crate p = T.ENTRY_CRATE (p, p)
  | entry_token Entry_Expr p = T.ENTRY_EXPR (p, p)
  | entry_token Entry_Type p = T.ENTRY_TYPE (p, p)
  | entry_token Entry_Id p = T.ENTRY_ID (p, p)
  | entry_token Entry_Body p = T.ENTRY_BODY (p, p)

fun entry_stream entry raw_lex pos eof_pos =
  let
    val eof_tok = T.EOF (eof_pos, eof_pos)
    val queue = Unsynchronized.ref [entry_token entry (pos 0)]
    val eof_seen = Unsynchronized.ref false
    fun next () =
      (case !queue of
         t :: ts => (queue := ts; t)
       | [] =>
           if !eof_seen then eof_tok
           else
             let val tok = raw_lex ()
             in if P.sameToken (tok, eof_tok) then (eof_seen := true; eof_tok)
                else tok end)
  in P.Stream.streamify next end

(* Runs the parser on "source" from the given entry point; "mk_err" makes the
   parser's error callback from the parse's state. Every parse creates its own
   state. *)
fun parse mk_err entry ctxt source =
  let
    val st = AdaSpark_State.init ctxt source
    val err = mk_err st
    val input_text = Lex_yacc_state.text_of (#base st)
    val consumed = Unsynchronized.ref false
    fun input_string _ = if !consumed then ""
      else (consumed := true; input_text)
    val raw_lex = AdaSpark.AdaSparkLex.makeLexer input_string st
    val pos = Lex_yacc_state.get_pos (#base st)
    val eof_pos = pos (String.size input_text)
    val stream = entry_stream entry raw_lex pos eof_pos
    val (result, _) = P.parse (0, stream, err, st)
      handle Fail msg => (err (msg, pos 0, pos 0); raise Fail msg)
    val _ = (case !(#lex_error st) of SOME (msg, p) =>
             err (msg, p, p) | NONE => ())
  in result end

fun parse_loud entry ctxt source =
  parse (fn st => Lex_yacc_state.print_error (#base st)) entry ctxt source

(* The silent variant the "_reject" commands use: a locally declared
   exception, not the library's "print_error" (which reports PIDE error markup
   before raising, and raises an exception Isabelle/ML cannot reliably catch
   by identity across the SML sandbox boundary). *)
exception Rejected of string
fun quiet_error (s : string, _ : Position.T, _ : Position.T) = raise Rejected s

fun parse_quiet entry ctxt source = parse (K quiet_error) entry ctxt source

end
\<close>

end
